            "count": 0,
            "is_markdown": false,
            "bug_id": 19291,
            "text": "format(<POSIXlt>, usetz = TRUE) appends \" \" and the zone name to its strftime() output with two unchecked strcat() calls into a 2049-byte stack buffer. A format whose output is 2045 to 2048 bytes writes the zone past the end of the buffer, and a long \"zone\" component (or \"tzone\" attribute, for an object without a zone component) writes any number of bytes past it. Both abort R 4.6.1 and R-devel (r90850); an ASan build reports a stack-buffer-overflow in do_formatPOSIXlt().\n\nReproducible example: attached as format-posixlt-usetz-repro.R; both cases abort R, expected an error or a result.\n\nAnalysis:\n\nIn do_formatPOSIXlt() (src/main/datetime.c), buff is filled by strftime(buff, 2049, ...) and the usetz branch then strcat()s the zone without a length check. Until r83243 (R 4.3.0) the buffer was 300 bytes with a 256-byte strftime() limit, which left room for a short zone, so only the long-zone case is old.\n\nProposed patch: attached as format-posixlt-usetz.diff. It computes the appended length and signals the existing \"output string exceeded 2048 bytes\" error when the result would not fit; a regression test is included. Found by OSS-Fuzz.\n\nThe patch is also submitted as https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/pull/457, where CI results can be seen.",
